{"name":"Apple Slice","hex":"#f1f0bf","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"apple","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A common, firm, round fruit produced by a tree of the genus Malus.","The fruit of the tree Malus domestica, chiefly with a green, red, or yellow skin, cultivated in temperate climates for cidermaking, cooking, and eating. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make (something) appear like an apple (noun sense 1.1).","To become like an apple.\n\n To collect fir-cones.\n Of a flower bud or vegetable (especially a root vegetable): to grow into the shape of an apple."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/apple"},{"term":"slice","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["That which is thin and broad.","A thin, broad piece cut off."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cut into slices.","To cut with an edge using a drawing motion."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slice"}],"entries":[{"title":"Slice (drink)","blocks":[{"text":"Slice is a line of primarily fruit-flavored soft drinks originally manufactured by PepsiCo and currently manufactured as a low-sugar prebiotic soda by Suja Life. Slice was first introduced in 1984 but discontinued by PepsiCo in North America in the late 2000s."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/02/Slice_drink_brand_logo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Slice_(drink)","wikidata":"Q7540223"},{"title":"Apple","blocks":[{"text":"An apple is the round, edible fruit of an apple tree. Fruit trees of the orchard or domestic apple, the most widely grown in the genus, are cultivated worldwide. The tree originated in Central Asia, where its wild ancestor, Malus sieversii, is still found. Apples have been grown for thousands of years in Eurasia before they were introduced to the American continent by European colonists. Apples have cultural significance in many mythologies and religions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Pink_lady_and_cross_section.jpg/330px-Pink_lady_and_cross_section.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apple","wikidata":"Q89"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Mymomisnotreal%27s_Picture_of_the_original_%22Slice%22_flavor.jpg/500px-Mymomisnotreal%27s_Picture_of_the_original_%22Slice%22_flavor.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Mymomisnotreal%27s_Picture_of_the_original_%22Slice%22_flavor.jpg/500px-Mymomisnotreal%27s_Picture_of_the_original_%22Slice%22_flavor.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMymomisnotreal's_Picture_of_the_original_%22Slice%22_flavor.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Malus_domestica_a1.jpg/500px-Malus_domestica_a1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Malus_domestica_a1.jpg/500px-Malus_domestica_a1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMalus_domestica_a1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Apple_Blossom_%40_Manali.jpg/500px-Apple_Blossom_%40_Manali.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Apple_Blossom_%40_Manali.jpg/960px-Apple_Blossom_%40_Manali.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Apple_Blossom_%40_Manali.jpg/500px-Apple_Blossom_%40_Manali.jpg?utm_